{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Compute length of longest palindromic subsequence in s.\n\n    Treat characters exactly as provided (no normalization of case or whitespace).\n    Return 0 when s is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of s[i...j]\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromes of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for lengths from 2 to n\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If characters match, they contribute 2 to the LPS.\n                # Add LPS of the inner substring s[i+1...j-1].\n                # If length is 2 (inner substring is empty), dp[i+1][j-1] will be 0.\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1]\n            else:\n                # If characters don't match, take the maximum of excluding s[i] or s[j].\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
