{"task_id": "Mbpp/312", "solution": "import math\n\ndef volume_cone(radius: float, height: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the volume of a cone given its radius and height.\n    Raises TypeError if radius or height are not numeric.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(radius, (int, float)):\n        raise TypeError(\"Radius must be a numeric value (int or float).\")\n    if not isinstance(height, (int, float)):\n        raise TypeError(\"Height must be a numeric value (int or float).\")\n\n    volume = (1/3) * math.pi * (radius ** 2) * height\n    return volume"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/391", "solution": "class ValidationError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for validation errors in list conversion.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\ndef convert_list_dictionary(*lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Accepts two or more lists and returns a list of nested dictionaries.\n    Each item in the output list corresponds to an index, with the first list's\n    element as the top-level key and subsequent lists forming nested keys.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(lists) < 2:\n        raise ValidationError(\"At least two input lists are required.\")\n\n    expected_len = len(lists[0])\n    for l in lists:\n        if len(l) != expected_len:\n            raise ValidationError(\"All input lists must have the same length.\")\n\n    if expected_len == 0:\n        return []\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(expected_len):\n        current_nested_dict = lists[-1][i]\n        # Iterate backwards from the second to the second-to-last list\n        # to build the nested structure.\n        for j in range(len(lists) - 2, 0, -1):\n            current_nested_dict = {lists[j][i]: current_nested_dict}\n        \n        # The top-level key comes from the first list.\n        item = {lists[0][i]: current_nested_dict}\n        result.append(item)\n\n    return result"}
